WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:14.500
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:15.468 --> 00:00:18.001
[straining]

00:00:18.001 --> 00:00:19.929
Yeah, I can't lift this.

00:00:19.929 --> 00:00:24.249
We should've designed this suit to have
pneumatic jacks built into the arms.

00:00:24.249 --> 00:00:25.701
Can I climb out of here?

00:00:26.464 --> 00:00:28.878
No, it doesn't reach the ceiling.

00:00:28.878 --> 00:00:32.301
Maybe I should stop this gas
filling the room, huh?

00:00:32.301 --> 00:00:36.441
I'm glad they have a valve here
to stop it; this must happen often.

00:00:36.441 --> 00:00:38.176
Oh, this is new.

00:00:38.176 --> 00:00:40.601
Yeah, this was sealed;
there was no hatch.

00:00:41.651 --> 00:00:45.364
Why would we build a ladder
going up to a grate you can't open?

00:00:45.364 --> 00:00:47.298
Is this a dungeon?

00:00:47.298 --> 00:00:48.632
Yeah, maybe.

00:00:48.632 --> 00:00:49.694
[sneezes]

00:00:49.694 --> 00:00:52.029
Like, the ladder is just to
tease the prisoners

00:00:52.029 --> 00:00:54.456
to thinking they can see
the sky through the grate,

00:00:54.456 --> 00:00:57.571
except it's a trick because
they're still inside a dome.

00:00:57.571 --> 00:00:58.785
SCIENTIST: I seem to be
seriously wounded.

00:00:58.785 --> 00:01:00.009
Yeah, don't touch me.

00:01:00.009 --> 00:01:01.485
SCIENTIST: I don't think I can
last much longer.

00:01:01.485 --> 00:01:03.162
Well, this IS a dungeon.

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:03.790
SCIENTIST: STAAH!

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:04.300
What?

00:01:05.539 --> 00:01:08.554
Oh, I'm sorry! Were you using that ammo?!

00:01:08.554 --> 00:01:10.052
Could've fooled me!

00:01:10.052 --> 00:01:12.473
So, those are literally your last words?

00:01:12.473 --> 00:01:15.219
Screaming at somebody
not to touch your stuff.

00:01:15.219 --> 00:01:17.826
Boy, you lived a fulfilling life, huh?

00:01:17.826 --> 00:01:19.243
[strange yowling noise]

00:01:19.243 --> 00:01:20.889
[strange yowling noise]
Okay...

00:01:20.889 --> 00:01:23.805
[strange yowling noise]
that's definitely more than one ghost.

00:01:23.805 --> 00:01:25.033
What am I looking at?

00:01:25.965 --> 00:01:27.641
[Geiger counter ticking]
No!

00:01:27.641 --> 00:01:29.018
[Geiger counter ticking]
Hey, you're a witness!

00:01:29.018 --> 00:01:31.213
[Geiger counter ticking]

00:01:31.213 --> 00:01:33.666
[Geiger counter ticking]
Fuck, this even MORE radioactive.

00:01:33.666 --> 00:01:35.249
[Geiger counter ticking]
This is exactly the kind of clicking

00:01:35.249 --> 00:01:36.742
[Geiger counter ticking]
I don't want to be hearing.

00:01:36.742 --> 00:01:37.834
[Geiger counter ticking]
I don't like performing

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:39.862
[Geiger counter ticking]
Dance of the Geiger Counter.

00:01:39.862 --> 00:01:40.879
Hey, uhh...

00:01:40.879 --> 00:01:43.267
Oh, okay, you're busy. That's good.

00:01:44.635 --> 00:01:48.260
Oh, here we go! Oh, wow!

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:49.922
Perfect!

00:01:49.922 --> 00:01:52.978
I could use some popcorn for this!

00:01:52.978 --> 00:01:55.422
Might want to fire your gun there...

00:01:55.422 --> 00:01:56.353
No?

00:01:56.353 --> 00:01:58.769
Okay, that's just me.

00:01:58.769 --> 00:02:03.991
This guy is giving a performance!
I respect that.

00:02:03.991 --> 00:02:08.345
I should get a good grip in case
his body hits me on the way down.

00:02:08.345 --> 00:02:12.481
Ah hah! Someone's spying on me! I knew it!

00:02:12.481 --> 00:02:16.100
Or maybe he's motioning for me
to follow him but I'm not going to.

00:02:17.946 --> 00:02:19.234
Hey, what the hell?

00:02:22.098 --> 00:02:26.338
It was just a zombie making him move
around like it's a giant puppet show.

00:02:26.338 --> 00:02:28.693
I don't like the implications of this.

00:02:28.693 --> 00:02:32.722
All they've been doing so far is running
into walls and acting angry at the world,

00:02:32.722 --> 00:02:35.452
and now they're playing
Punch and Judy with the bodies.

00:02:35.452 --> 00:02:38.400
The other was dragging it around
like it was a teddy bear.

00:02:39.483 --> 00:02:43.033
I don't know if it's a sign of
growing intelligence or something else.

00:02:45.274 --> 00:02:48.000
Well, you don't disappoint!
You don't change a bit!

00:02:49.722 --> 00:02:52.494
I can always count on you to be horrible.

00:02:52.494 --> 00:02:54.234
Simple and horrible.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:55.797
[kzzt]

00:02:55.797 --> 00:02:56.634
Excuse me?

00:02:58.037 --> 00:03:02.328
I... thought I heard someone.
Someone green.

00:03:02.328 --> 00:03:06.815
Or, maybe I really have caught a bullet
in the head and I'm hearing colors now.

00:03:06.815 --> 00:03:09.327
I don't think synesthesia's contagious but

00:03:09.327 --> 00:03:12.432
the sky's the limit when
you've got head trauma.

00:03:12.432 --> 00:03:14.998
Anyway, if the zombies are
getting smarter,

00:03:14.998 --> 00:03:18.615
I think the next logical step is
for them to steal the soldiers' uniforms

00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:20.138
and pretend to be one of them.

00:03:20.138 --> 00:03:23.590
They would get shot, but the
soldiers shoot each other anyway.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:27.011
I estimate the zombies would
have about a 50% success rate

00:03:27.011 --> 00:03:29.312
at infiltrating us if they tried that.

00:03:29.312 --> 00:03:32.548
The soldiers would look at them
and think they're sick or...

00:03:32.548 --> 00:03:34.796
well, I don't know WHAT goes
through their heads.

00:03:34.796 --> 00:03:35.567
Ehh...

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.734
No, you go first! It's cool. I can wait.

00:03:46.182 --> 00:03:49.467
This is NOT a line I'm in a rush
to get through.

00:03:50.858 --> 00:03:53.843
It just really doesn't pay to be
in front here.

00:03:53.843 --> 00:03:57.135
If I thought I could pull it off,
I would put the zombie in MY suit

00:03:57.135 --> 00:03:58.768
and just march him out here.

00:03:58.768 --> 00:04:03.911
The military would kill him then say,
"Yep, we got Freeman. Our job's done here."

00:04:03.911 --> 00:04:06.632
I'm pretty sure they would buy it.

00:04:06.632 --> 00:04:12.109
I mean, look at-- Oh yeah, I almost forgot.
Option 3: the most likely option.

00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:13.133
[teleportation sound]
Yah!

00:04:14.979 --> 00:04:17.111
People keep interrupting me!

00:04:17.111 --> 00:04:21.285
But, yeah, Option 3 is the
military is rock stupid.

00:04:21.285 --> 00:04:23.482
Like frightening stupid.

00:04:23.482 --> 00:04:30.023
Like crash-planes-into-buildings-bomb-your-
own-troops-and-shoot-half-your-squad stupid.

00:04:30.023 --> 00:04:33.667
"Duh... whoops! I killed the
wrong guy again!"

00:04:34.921 --> 00:04:38.701
Like maybe the only soldiers
that aren't literally retarded

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:42.000
either have non-combative duty
or else they're overseas.

00:04:44.564 --> 00:04:47.239
So, what I'm seeing is all that's left.

00:04:47.239 --> 00:04:49.000
This isn't THAT hard.

00:04:49.616 --> 00:04:52.367
I mean, c'mon, these
are walking green Tasers.

00:04:54.871 --> 00:04:57.534
I don't think I want
to wait on THIS crowd.

00:04:58.946 --> 00:05:03.326
See, this is what I mean. That guy was just
walking casually in the center of the room,

00:05:03.326 --> 00:05:04.570
exposed.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:09.503
Did he have headphones on? Have music
playing so loud you can't hear gunshots?

00:05:09.503 --> 00:05:12.697
They might sell earbuds like
that. I'm not sure.

00:05:12.697 --> 00:05:16.192
Must've been pretty good music since
I'm assuming he had his eyes closed

00:05:16.192 --> 00:05:19.174
since there were green bolts of
electricity flying around.

00:05:19.174 --> 00:05:21.216
Or maybe that just happened to fit the beat

00:05:21.216 --> 00:05:24.951
so that he didn't give it much
conscious thought until it was too late.

00:05:24.951 --> 00:05:27.165
Music soothes even the...

00:05:27.165 --> 00:05:31.236
spaced-out Marine who forgot he
was in the middle of a warzone, apparently.

00:05:31.236 --> 00:05:32.867
Shit, if I could document this,

00:05:32.867 --> 00:05:36.984
I could publish this as a research
paper on the way out the door!

00:05:36.984 --> 00:05:38.686
Because, that's how I roll.

00:05:38.686 --> 00:05:42.825
I lose my job, I have a research
paper before I'm out the building!

00:05:42.825 --> 00:05:47.244
No, wait, shit. I'm a fugitive and
I killed a lot of people. I forgot.

00:05:47.244 --> 00:05:50.685
So, I guess that guard broke the
door because he was bored.

00:05:50.685 --> 00:05:51.789
Where do I go now?

00:05:51.789 --> 00:05:53.004
[door buzzes]

00:05:53.004 --> 00:05:57.052
C'mon! There has to be a
ventilation shaft here somewhere.

00:05:57.052 --> 00:05:59.367
What's this? Is this a security station?

00:06:00.942 --> 00:06:05.485
No, this is for mixing music.
Maybe the guard's a DJ on the side.

00:06:05.485 --> 00:06:08.699
There HAS to be a shaft.
We have great airflow here.

00:06:08.699 --> 00:06:13.184
In all my time at Black Mesa I've never
seen anyone suffocate in their office

00:06:13.184 --> 00:06:16.126
or black out because
of carbon dioxide poisoning.

00:06:16.126 --> 00:06:18.782
That hasn't been true at all
jobs I've worked at.

00:06:18.782 --> 00:06:20.615
Oh, you broke it good, huh?

00:06:20.615 --> 00:06:21.242
How did--WAHH!

00:06:21.242 --> 00:06:22.411
[vortigaunts charging up]

00:06:22.411 --> 00:06:22.810
[vortigaunt bolt]

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:28.142
Oh, so you HERDED them there! You really
ARE a space rancher! That's awesome!

00:06:28.142 --> 00:06:31.180
Well, I hate to do this to you,
but I have to put them down.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:32.731
I need you to step over here.

00:06:32.731 --> 00:06:34.135
GUARD: We might live longer if
we work together.

00:06:34.135 --> 00:06:35.787
Yeah, c'mon waggle-jaw.

00:06:35.787 --> 00:06:38.895
I'll be humane about this... not
that I care about that,

00:06:38.895 --> 00:06:41.842
but I do care about quick so our
goals are the same.

00:06:41.842 --> 00:06:43.934
Oh, what the hell?
How did I miss that?

00:06:44.905 --> 00:06:48.870
Okay, that wasn't supposed to happen
and now I've spooked the animals,

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:51.013
so let's just do this the
traditional way.

00:06:51.013 --> 00:06:53.845
Our colleague down in the
dungeon would've wanted this.

00:06:53.845 --> 00:06:56.739
Or, maybe he just wanted to be
buried with his shotgun shells,

00:06:56.739 --> 00:06:58.699
but what do we care? He's dead.

00:06:58.699 --> 00:06:59.984
Now, does this work?

00:06:59.984 --> 00:07:02.173
Yep! Here we go! Are you
watching this?

00:07:02.773 --> 00:07:03.500
Oh, yeah!

00:07:05.812 --> 00:07:06.434
Ho!

00:07:08.366 --> 00:07:09.133
Whoa!

00:07:09.974 --> 00:07:10.467
Christ...

00:07:11.079 --> 00:07:13.275
I got a little carried away there.

00:07:13.275 --> 00:07:15.359
I'm glad nothing ricocheted at me.

00:07:15.359 --> 00:07:17.968
And now the job gets more complicated.

00:07:20.112 --> 00:07:22.724
See, it was better when you were
all packed together.

00:07:22.724 --> 00:07:25.316
I mean, c'mon, safety in
numbers, right?

00:07:25.316 --> 00:07:26.100
[vortigese]

00:07:27.371 --> 00:07:28.734
Exactly.

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:33.067
Eh, I spoke too soon.

00:07:35.823 --> 00:07:37.665
Now, are there any more of you here?

00:07:37.665 --> 00:07:40.099
Drinking some soda? No?

00:07:40.099 --> 00:07:42.417
Well, I have to say I'm impressed.

00:07:42.417 --> 00:07:46.088
That guy herded six of them into
this hallway. That takes talent.

00:07:46.088 --> 00:07:48.618
I wasn't the only one thinking
outside the box.

00:07:48.618 --> 00:07:50.587
Y'know, one of my
regrets about leaving here

00:07:50.587 --> 00:07:53.296
is I didn't get to do all the
experiments I wanted.

00:07:53.296 --> 00:07:56.434
Like I wanted to slip Rohypnol
into the coffee pot for a few weeks

00:07:56.434 --> 00:07:58.714
and observe how that affected
people's work habits.

00:07:58.714 --> 00:07:59.567
[scientist screaming]
Waah!

00:08:00.764 --> 00:08:01.548
Oh.

00:08:02.129 --> 00:08:03.685
You're not real.

00:08:03.685 --> 00:08:04.367
Ha ha.

00:08:05.249 --> 00:08:07.246
Man, you two aren't dead yet?

00:08:07.246 --> 00:08:09.670
Oh, right, I just saved you.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:10.687
You're welcome.

00:08:10.687 --> 00:08:12.143
You can pay me, y'know.

00:08:12.143 --> 00:08:13.277
I take cash.
SCIENTIST: Freeman!

00:08:13.277 --> 00:08:15.107
SCIENTIST: Who would've thought
you'd still be alive!

00:08:15.107 --> 00:08:18.381
Oh, funny man! You're saying that to me!

00:08:18.381 --> 00:08:21.448
Well, you ARE cowering in my
presence appropriately

00:08:21.448 --> 00:08:23.532
so I guess I can't be too hard on you.

00:08:23.532 --> 00:08:25.661
Okay, you get to live.

00:08:25.661 --> 00:08:29.550
But I'm going to need you to stand there and
smack yourself in the head repeatedly, alright?

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:30.875
GUARD: Bring it on!

00:08:30.875 --> 00:08:32.131
Who's he talking to?

00:08:32.131 --> 00:08:33.234
There's no one here.
GUARD: Hey, Gordon.

00:08:33.234 --> 00:08:35.087
GUARD: It can't get any worse
than this, can it?

00:08:35.087 --> 00:08:38.404
Uh, no. This is the absolute
worst it can get.

00:08:38.404 --> 00:08:41.161
I can't imagine anything worse
than what you've seen.

00:08:41.161 --> 00:08:42.791
GUARD: You have any idea what's going on?

00:08:42.791 --> 00:08:46.109
Oh, my God. You people are all hopeless.

00:08:46.109 --> 00:08:50.052
You say that like a bored kid
wanting to know what time lunch is.

00:08:50.052 --> 00:08:51.524
I can't help you.

00:08:51.524 --> 00:08:54.014
You shouldn't have even
made it this far in life.

00:08:54.014 --> 00:08:57.956
You lack basic problem-solving
skills. That's so fundamental.

00:08:57.956 --> 00:08:59.751
You need to be in a home.

00:08:59.751 --> 00:09:02.979
Okay, good. This doesn't even
have a code so I don't need you.

00:09:02.979 --> 00:09:05.383
You're going to die here. I'm sorry.

00:09:05.383 --> 00:09:06.142
There's no way

00:09:06.142 --> 00:09:07.297
[fzzt]

00:09:07.297 --> 00:09:10.534
Shit, something's happening. I
think I'm having flashbacks.

00:09:11.752 --> 00:09:12.632
HEADCRABBED SCIENTIST: Is
someone there?

00:09:12.632 --> 00:09:13.823
Oh, God....

00:09:13.823 --> 00:09:15.873
HEADCRABBED SCIENTIST: I... I
can't see a thing...

00:09:15.873 --> 00:09:17.667
Okay, I'll try to get it off.

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:19.736
Shit, did I hit him?

00:09:19.736 --> 00:09:21.220
I don't want to think about this.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:21.734
[houndeye squeals]

00:09:22.714 --> 00:09:25.200
Yeah, you're next, you hopping maggot!

00:09:25.745 --> 00:09:28.100
WHAT MAKES YOU THINK I WANT YOUR ADVICE?!

00:09:29.307 --> 00:09:33.909
Shit... everyone's trying to tell me
what to do; ghost, aliens, people,

00:09:33.909 --> 00:09:36.316
they're never going to stop
until they're all dead.

00:09:36.316 --> 00:09:37.234
Except the ghost.

00:09:37.869 --> 00:09:38.834
OHHH!

00:09:39.872 --> 00:09:41.377
MOTHERFUCKER!

00:09:41.377 --> 00:09:43.155
YOU'RE IN ON IT, TOO!

00:09:43.155 --> 00:09:44.067
AND YOU!

00:09:45.116 --> 00:09:46.342
They ambushed me!

00:09:46.342 --> 00:09:48.705
They ARE getting more intelligent!

00:09:48.705 --> 00:09:50.987
That was an honest-to-God trap!

00:09:50.987 --> 00:09:53.280
I think the hopper was just bait!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.176
He lured me in there!

00:09:55.176 --> 00:09:57.719
Well, that's one problem solved.

00:09:57.719 --> 00:09:59.006
Guess I hit him after all.

00:09:59.006 --> 00:10:01.810
[door buzzes]
Oh, come ON!

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:03.885
Shit, maybe he ran in there.

00:10:03.885 --> 00:10:06.848
Well, will the guard help me
after what I said?

00:10:06.848 --> 00:10:11.123
He may be too stupid to be offended,
but he may not even know the code.

00:10:11.123 --> 00:10:13.167
Screw it. I don't want the drama.

00:10:13.167 --> 00:10:16.110
I'll take the shaft that looks
like an exposed ribcage.

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:18.310
If I have to wrestle with the
maggot thing in here,

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:21.022
I'm pretty sure I'm going to
remember that the rest of my life.

00:10:21.022 --> 00:10:25.186
I mean, I'm going to remember a lot of
this, but some things cut deeper than others.

00:10:25.186 --> 00:10:26.624
[thumping, gargantua growling]

00:10:26.624 --> 00:10:31.735
Oh... wide load coming through...
everybody back up.

00:10:31.735 --> 00:10:33.167
[gargantua roaring]
Uh...

00:10:34.167 --> 00:10:38.602
Oh, shit. Looks like the bridge
clearance was too low.

00:10:38.602 --> 00:10:42.618
Maybe he'll smash a way out of
here and I can just follow in his wake.

00:10:42.618 --> 00:10:45.465
And we have locked blast doors here, too,

00:10:45.465 --> 00:10:48.557
because, apparently we
anticipated this sort of thing.

00:10:48.557 --> 00:10:51.362
I mean, the ceiling was built
high enough for him.

00:10:51.362 --> 00:10:54.771
You could perform a
full trapeze act in this room.

00:10:54.771 --> 00:10:57.150
Well, this is pretty convenient, really.

00:10:57.150 --> 00:11:01.346
Yeah, why not? I'll give this a try as
soon as the electricity dies down some.

00:11:01.346 --> 00:11:04.403
Then I won't be stunned before
dropping down twenty feet.

00:11:04.403 --> 00:11:08.367
Chuggachuggachuggachuggachuggachuggachugga
chuggachuggachuggachuggachuggachugga!

00:11:08.866 --> 00:11:10.379
Ah, that's better.

00:11:10.379 --> 00:11:12.560
But now we have an air vent dragon.

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:14.570
Wait, no, too loud.

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:15.585
FUCK YOU!

00:11:15.585 --> 00:11:18.601
I HATE YOU AND I'M GONNA GO KILL
YOUR WHOLE FAMILY NOW!

00:11:19.493 --> 00:11:20.938
Y'know, the joke's gonna be on me

00:11:20.938 --> 00:11:24.524
if I find out later that these things
actually taste good when cooked

00:11:24.524 --> 00:11:26.436
and we're raising them in a few years,

00:11:26.436 --> 00:11:28.474
but I just don't see
that--WAAAH!

00:11:28.474 --> 00:11:30.047
Oh, lucky...

00:11:30.047 --> 00:11:32.271
I should do something...!
SCIENTIST: Get back!

00:11:32.271 --> 00:11:34.378
[scientist screaming]

00:11:34.378 --> 00:11:37.408
I'm kind of freezing up here!
What am I doing?!

00:11:37.408 --> 00:11:39.067
This is good, I think!

00:11:41.503 --> 00:11:44.400
No, this isn't working!
Let's do it some more!

00:11:45.226 --> 00:11:46.017
C'mon!

00:11:46.017 --> 00:11:46.517
God!

00:11:46.517 --> 00:11:48.049
GUARD: HEY! AAAAAAH!

00:11:48.049 --> 00:11:49.754
Get out of there, moron!

00:11:49.754 --> 00:11:51.523
Oh, fuuuck!

00:11:51.523 --> 00:11:53.058
THIS IS BULLSHIT!

00:11:53.058 --> 00:11:55.608
EVERYTHING I'VE BEEN DOING
UP UNTIL THIS POINT

00:11:55.608 --> 00:11:59.444
WAS SO I WOULD NOT BE
